Feature: Functional Onboarding + Logic Layer Connection for FinanzasDaniel v0.2

CONTEXT
The app compiled successfully (v0.1) with premium UI but no data persistence or logic. 
This feature wires everything together and adds the onboarding flow.

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
USER STORY 1 — First launch onboarding
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

As a first-time user, I want to set up the app through a guided flow so that 
it knows my financial reality before showing me anything.

STEP 1 — Welcome splash (non-interactive, 2.5s or tap to skip)
  - Large emoji animation: 🏍️ → 💰 → 📈 (morphs with spring)
  - Headline: "Hola. Vamos a ordenar tus finanzas."
  - Subline: "4 preguntas. 2 minutos. Sin excusas."
  - Auto-advances or tap anywhere

STEP 2 — Ingreso mensual
  - Question: "¿Cuánto entra cada mes?"
  - Large hero number input (SF Mono, 52pt): "$0" → user types amount
  - Subtext: "Escribe tu salario neto — lo que llega a tu cuenta."
  - Below input: "¿Qué día te pagan?" → segmented or scroll picker (1–31)
  - Validation: amount > 0, day 1–31. CTA disabled until valid.
  - CTA: "Eso es todo por aquí →"

STEP 3 — Gastos fijos
  - Question: "¿Qué gastos fijos tienes?"
  - Subtext: "Arriendo, créditos, suscripciones... lo que sale sí o sí."
  - Preset chips to tap (multi-select, adds with default amount):
    [Icetex] [Arriendo] [Crédito] [Netflix] [Spotify] [Gym] [+ Agregar]
  - Each selected chip expands to inline editable row:
    [Icono] [Nombre]  [$Monto]  [Día de pago: DD]  [×]
  - "Agregar" → inline empty row to fill
  - User can set: nombre, monto, día del mes en que cae el pago
  - Minimum 0 fixed expenses (can skip). CTA always enabled.
  - CTA: "Guardados →"

STEP 4 — Meta / Proyecto de ahorro
  - Question: "¿Hacia qué estás ahorrando?"
  - Subtext: "Puede ser una moto, un viaje, un colchón. Lo que sea."
  - Goal card editor (inline):
    - Emoji picker (grid de 40 emojis categorizados)
    - Nombre (TextField)
    - Monto meta ($)  
    - Fecha límite (DatePicker — optional, toggle "¿Tiene fecha límite?")
    - Aporte mensual ($) — con hint: "¿Cuánto puedes apartar cada mes?"
  - "Agregar otra meta +" link below card (same inline editor, stacked)
  - Pre-filled suggestion: 🏍️ "BMW G 310 GS" $13.250.000 — user can edit or delete
  - Minimum 1 goal required. CTA disabled until at least 1 goal has name + amount.
  - CTA: "Ya casi →"

STEP 5 — Budget suggestion + notification permission
  - Headline: "Aquí va tu panorama, Daniel."
  - Show calculated breakdown card (read-only):
    ┌─────────────────────────────────────┐
    │ Tu ingreso mensual      $2.450.000  │
    │ Gastos fijos           −$1.300.000  │
    │ Aporte a metas         −$1.200.000  │
    │ Colchón (10%)           −$245.000   │
    ├─────────────────────────────────────┤
    │ Para gastos del día a día $305.000  │  ← accent-mint, large
    └─────────────────────────────────────┘
  - Below card: "Este es el presupuesto que calculamos para tus gastos 
    variables. No te preguntamos — lo calculamos por ti."
    [info icon] → expandable: explains the formula in plain Spanish
  
  - Below that: notification opt-in card
    Icon: bell.badge.fill (accent-mint)
    Title: "¿Te avisamos cuando toca pagar?"
    Body: "Te recordamos un día antes de cada gasto fijo y te preguntamos 
           si ya lo hiciste."
    CTA: "Sí, activar notificaciones" (primary button)
    Secondary: "Ahora no" (text button, text-secondary)
  
  - Main CTA: "Entrar →" (enabled regardless of notification choice)
  - On tap: mark onboarding_complete = true → navigate to MainTabView with 
    .transition(.asymmetric(insertion:.move(edge:.trailing), removal:.opacity))

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
USER STORY 2 — Stats card con comparativa mes anterior
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

As a user on the Dashboard, I want to see how this month compares to last month 
so I can know if I'm improving.

STATS CARD (in DashboardView, after the Hero Card):
  - Title: "vs. mes anterior"
  - 3 metrics side by side:
    1. Gastos variables: "$303.000  ↓12%" (green if less than last month)
    2. Ahorro logrado:   "$600.000  ↑8%"  (green if more)
    3. Saldo libre:      "$847.000  ↑5%"  (green if more)
  - Each metric: value in SF Mono + delta chip (↑/↓ + %) colored semantically
  - Below metrics: horizontal bar chart (SwiftUI Canvas, no Charts framework)
    Two bars per category (current month = solid, last month = 30% opacity)
    Categories: Comida / Transporte / Ocio / Otros
    Bar height max 80pt, animated on appear
  - Empty state (first month): "Aún no hay mes anterior para comparar. 
    Vuelve en [X] days." — shown with a dotted border card

DATA MODEL — MonthlySnapshot:
  @Model class MonthlySnapshot {
    var id: UUID
    var year: Int
    var month: Int          // 1–12
    var totalIncome: Double
    var totalFixedExpenses: Double
    var totalVariableExpenses: Double
    var totalSaved: Double  // sum of contributions that month
    var expensesByCategory: [String: Double]  // category rawValue: amount
    var createdAt: Date
  }
  
  Auto-created: on first launch of a new calendar month, snapshot the previous month's data.

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
USER STORY 3 — Fixed expense payment notifications
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

As a user, I want to be reminded the day before a fixed expense is due and be 
asked if I already paid it, so I never miss a payment or forget to track it.

NOTIFICATION BEHAVIOR:
  - Scheduled: every month on (dueDay - 1) at 8:00 AM
  - Title: "💸 Mañana toca pagar [Nombre]"
  - Body: "Son $[Monto]. ¿Ya lo hiciste?"
  - Actions (UNNotificationAction):
    - "Sí, ya pagué" (identifier: "PAID") — foreground: false, destructive: false
    - "Recordar mañana" (identifier: "SNOOZE") — foreground: false

  PAID action handler:
    - Create Expense record: amount = fixedExpense.amount, category = fixedExpense.category,
      merchant = fixedExpense.name, source = .wallet, date = today, note = "Pago automático desde notificación"
    - Mark fixedExpense.paidThisMonth = true
    - Show local confirmation banner (UNNotificationContent, no app open needed)

  SNOOZE action handler:
    - Schedule new one-time notification for tomorrow same time
    - No Expense record created

  RESCHEDULE LOGIC:
    - All recurring notifications rescheduled on:
      1. App foreground after midnight of a new month
      2. User edits a FixedExpense (delete old, create new trigger)
    
  ADD to FixedExpense model:
    var paidThisMonth: Bool = false
    var lastPaidDate: Date?

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
USER STORY 4 — AppState wiring (UI ↔ Logic)
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

As a developer, the app needs a central state object that all views read from 
so the UI reflects real data at all times.

AppState (@Observable singleton):
  var monthlyIncome: Double           // from UserDefaults
  var payDay: Int                     // from UserDefaults
  var suggestedVariableBudget: Double // computed, cached in UserDefaults
  var currentMonthExpenses: Double    // live sum from SwiftData query
  var currentMonthSaved: Double       // live sum of Contribution this month
  var activeGoals: [SavingsGoal]      // live query
  var currentMonthSnapshot: MonthlySnapshot?
  var previousMonthSnapshot: MonthlySnapshot?
  
  func recalculateSuggestedBudget()   // runs after any fixedExpense or goal change
  func scheduleAllNotifications()     // runs after onboarding + any fixedExpense edit
  func snapshotPreviousMonthIfNeeded() // runs on app foreground

WIRING CHECKLIST (agent must verify each):
  ☐ GoalsView reads from AppState.activeGoals (live, not static)
  ☐ GoalDetailView slider updates monthlyContribution and triggers recalculateSuggestedBudget()
  ☐ ExpensesView reads live SwiftData query filtered by current month
  ☐ AddExpenseSheet inserts to SwiftData + triggers currentMonthExpenses update
  ☐ Dashboard Hero Card reads AppState.currentMonthExpenses, .monthlyIncome, fixedExpenses sum
  ☐ Stats card reads currentMonthSnapshot vs previousMonthSnapshot
  ☐ Budget progress bar = currentMonthExpenses / suggestedVariableBudget
  ☐ AddContributionSheet updates goal.savedAmount + creates Contribution record + updates currentMonthSaved
  ☐ FixedExpense edit → rescheduleAllNotifications()
  ☐ Onboarding completion → AppState populated + notifications scheduled + transition to MainTabView
